# HY320 (MagCubic) -- board base. One unit, its owner's, dumped in full over
# ADB on 31.10.2026; nothing of ours has run on it yet.
#
# Same shape as hy310_defconfig and hy300_pro_defconfig: this file says what
# the hardware is, a role fragment in configs/fragments/ says what a build is
# for, and build/uboot-build.sh merges the two (docs/uboot/README.md, "Which
# defconfig"). Everything outside the DRAM block, the device tree name, the
# identification string and CONFIG_H713_BOARD_HY320 is the HY300 Pro's base,
# which is the HY310's minus HS200 -- see below.
#
# **No image is shipped for this board.** It is below `verified`
# (boards/hy320, boards/README.md honesty rule). The only build this base is
# meant for is the stage 5 *test image*, built on purpose (`--test-image`),
# named `-TEST`, and flashed by that owner alone. The unit has no UART, so
# every choice below takes the stock behaviour over a guess.
#
# Where the values come from:
#   - the DRAM block is this board's own: the 24 words of the vendor boot0 at
#     LBA 16 of the owner's dump (installer/h713/profiles/hy320.py, "dram"),
#     equal to the HY350 image's word for word. Nothing in it is borrowed,
#     with one deliberate exception, para2 and tpr13: the boot0 at LBA 16
#     says 0x00000000 / 0x34010100, the second boot0 copy at LBA 256 of the
#     same eMMC says 0x04000000 / 0xb4016103 -- the pair the vendor flash
#     tool writes, and the pair every working base in this fork runs
#     (hy310, l018, hy300_pro). This file takes the LBA 256 pair.
#   - CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=792 is the boot0's own clock, and the HY310's. At 792
#     the DDR3 path takes the same branches as on the HY310 (below the
#     800 MHz speed-bin split, above the clk > 672 PHY arm of
#     iw12_phy_train()), so nothing in it is new.
#   - tpr11/tpr12 0x44440000/0x00005555 are this board's (and the HY350's,
#     HY300 T08's and HY300 Pro's); the HY310 runs 0x44340000/0x00006666.
#   - tpr0..tpr2 are in the file for completeness only: the DDR3 arm of
#     iw12_set_timing() in arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50iw12.c never reads
#     them; only the LPDDR3 arm unpacks them.
#   - DX_ODT, DX_DRI and CA_DRI are not part of the 24-word boot0 block: not
#     this board's, the values every H713 base in the fork carries.
#   - no CONFIG_MMC_HS200_SUPPORT. The stock eMMC node does offer
#     mmc-hs200-1_8v (and hs400, 200 MHz), but HS200 with this driver's
#     tuning has been run on the HY310 only (644feba7e43: "The other H713
#     boards keep MMC high speed until someone with one of them reports");
#     l018 carries it because it is the HY310's base. A board without a
#     console takes the 52 MHz that every H713 board here has booted with.
#   - the device tree is sun50i-h713-hy320, an include of the bench board's
#     plus model and compatible -- the pattern of the HY310's and HY300 Pro's.
#   - CONFIG_H713_BOARD_HY320 gives project 0x30 this board's own panel row
#     (its 2200x1125 raster at 164 MHz, not the HY310's 2128x1120 at 143 MHz)
#     and drives only the panel lines its stock tree names (PH19, PH16, PH15;
#     PF6 is this board's SD card detect). See arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig.
CONFIG_ARM=y
CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320"
CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=792
CONFIG_SPL=y
CONFIG_IDENT_STRING=" HY320"
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_ODT=0x03030303
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_DX_DRI=0x0e0e0e0e
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_CA_DRI=0x1c12
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ODT_EN=0x1
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_ZQ=0x007b7bfb
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA1=0x000010f4
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_PARA2=0x04000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR0=0x00001c70
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR1=0x00000040
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR2=0x00000018
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_MR3=0x00000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR0=0x004a2195
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR1=0x02423190
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR2=0x0008b061
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR3=0xb4787896
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR4=0x00000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR5=0x48484848
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x00000048
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR7=0x1620121e
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR8=0x00000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR9=0x00000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0x00000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR11=0x44440000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR12=0x00005555
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR13=0xb4016103
CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H713=y
CONFIG_H713_POWERON_LIGHT_FAN=y
CONFIG_H713_MIPS_BOOT=y
CONFIG_H713_BOARD_HY320=y
CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_H713_DDR3_STOCK=y
CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA=2
CONFIG_MMC0_CD_PIN=""
# CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
CONFIG_SUPPORT_EMMC_BOOT=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
# CONFIG_WATCHDOG is not set
CONFIG_WDT=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
# CONFIG_USB_ETHER is not set
CONFIG_CONSOLE_MUX=y
CONFIG_SYS_CONSOLE_IS_IN_ENV=y
CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM=y
# CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ACM_WAIT_FOR_CONNECTION is not set
CONFIG_SYSRESET=y
CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
CONFIG_CMD_POWEROFF=y
CONFIG_FASTBOOT_CMD_OEM_POWEROFF=y
# No "usb start" in the preboot, as on the HY310 since 15.09.: the host-side
# USB scan cost 2 to 5 s on every boot and nothing in the product boot reads a
# USB device (no keyboard, no USB boot medium; the installer role brings its
# own PREBOOT and uses the gadget, not the host). The kernel starts the
# controllers itself -- patch 0005a clears the HCI PHYs' SIDDQ bit, which is
# what "usb start" was standing in for. The two reboot-mode magics stay:
# "reboot fastboot" and "reboot bootloader" from Linux.
CONFIG_PREBOOT="if itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xfa57b007; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; run fastboot_mode; elif itest.l *0x0709011c == 0xb007c0de; then mw.l 0x0709011c 0; setenv bootdelay -1; fi"
# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC=y
CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET=0x700000
CONFIG_ENV_MMC_DEVICE_INDEX=1
CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x800
CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_DATA_PART_OFFSET=0x0
CONFIG_H713_VENDOR_CHAINLOAD=y
CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
# No serial console on the one HY320 we have (its owner will not open it): U-Boot
# records its own console output, and `h713_conlog` (arch/arm/mach-sunxi/
# h713_conlog.c) copies the record to memory so that bootcmd can leave it on the
# eMMC for Linux to read.
CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD=y
CONFIG_CONSOLE_RECORD_OUT_SIZE=0x40000
